From e83b6f3d286431196fe70df11daf312fc4b5836c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-d-robotics maintainers <maintainers@invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 03:11:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs: reserve a terminator byte for root-map names

The vendor 6.1 tree stores BTRFS root names in a 16-byte array, but
"BLOCK_GROUP_TREE" uses all 16 bytes before its NUL terminator.  Wrynose's
GCC detects the truncated initializer with CONFIG_WERROR enabled.

Reserve one more byte so every table entry remains a valid C string.  This
also prevents a root-name lookup from reading into the next table field.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 fs/btrfs/print-tree.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/print-tree.c b/fs/btrfs/print-tree.c
index e3cd02259a10..23e3c2af64ed 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/print-tree.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/print-tree.c
@@ -10,6 +10,6 @@
 struct root_name_map {
 	u64 id;
-	char name[16];
+	char name[17];
 };
 
 static const struct root_name_map root_map[] = {
-- 
2.43.0
